</style>

<style>
/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   HIDE THEME SECTIONS  ·  perfume pages only

   This snippet renders exclusively for the perfumes collection, so these
   rules are emitted nowhere else and can never touch another product.

   1. inspiration_banner   - duplicated by our own imagery below
   2. faq_section_Hnngqe   - our FAQ is below; two FAQ blocks on one page
   3. Description and parameters - renders broken on perfumes. The short_desc
      metafield emits list items that open with two <br>, so bullets appear
      with nothing beside them, and the ZLOŽENIE / VHODNÉ NA AKTIVITY
      headings arrive unstyled. The WHOLE block goes - including the
      Parametre column and the "Séria PATH Flow™" badge that sits inside it.
      That is intentional, not an oversight.

   1 and 2 match on the section KEY SUFFIX, scoped to .shopify-section, so
   neither section order nor the changing template-- prefix matters, and no
   inner accordion ids are caught.

   3 matches ids hardcoded in the theme template. Those are more stable than
   a generated section key - they do not change when templates or theme
   versions do.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
.shopify-section[id$="__inspiration_banner"],
.shopify-section[id$="__faq_section_Hnngqe"]{display:none}

/* Target the two elements DIRECTLY. Do not reach for the parent section.

   ⚠ Do NOT reintroduce  .shopify-section:has(#description-parameters-grid).
   It was tried on 2026-08-18 and took the entire product card down with it -
   gallery, title, price, add-to-cart, all gone. The reason: this theme puts
   "Description and parameters" INSIDE the same .shopify-section as the
   product card, not in a section of its own. Hiding the parent hides the
   whole thing.

   These two ids are hardcoded in the theme template, so they are stable
   across template and theme-version changes. A little empty vertical padding
   may remain where the block was - that is the safe trade.

   !important is deliberate. Verified on the live page 2026-08-18: without it
   the h2 hid but the grid did not (computed display stayed "grid"), so the
   theme wins that one - either with its own !important or by setting display
   inline from JS (the grid carries transition-all duration-300). !important
   covers both. This is the legitimate use of it: overriding third-party
   theme code we do not own. Do NOT copy this habit into #nfp rules. */
#description_and_parameters,
#description-parameters-grid{display:none!important}

/* The same short_desc metafield renders a SECOND time inside the buy box,
   under the "Bude sa vám páčiť" heading, and it is broken there too - the
   list items open with two <br>, so bullets appear with nothing beside them.
   Uncomment to hide that copy as well. Left off by default because it sits
   in the buy box, and removing content from there is a sales decision, not
   a cosmetic one. */
/* #short_description{display:none!important} */
</style>

<script>
/* ── Belt and braces for the block above ────────────────────────────────
   The CSS rules did not win on the live page: the h2 hid, the grid did not
   (computed display stayed "grid" even with !important). The grid lives
   inside <product-info> in the main product section, and the theme sets its
   display by a route a stylesheet rule cannot outrank.

   An INLINE style with !important is the top of the cascade, so this wins.
   Runs three times because <product-info> re-renders itself on variant
   change, which would otherwise restore the block.

   If you ever confirm the CSS alone is enough, delete this script - not the
   other way round. Do not remove both.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
(function(){
  var ids = ['description_and_parameters','description-parameters-grid'];
  /* add 'short_description' to hide the buy-box copy of the same metafield */
  function hide(){
    ids.forEach(function(id){
      var e = document.getElementById(id);
      if (e) e.style.setProperty('display','none','important');
    });
  }
  hide();
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', hide);
  }
  setTimeout(hide, 800);
  document.addEventListener('variant:change', hide);
})();
</script>


